course: dictionary
lesson: 11846
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Blown is one of them. Blow is a verb, and its past form is blown. «The leaves were blown across the playground.» Here blown means pushed along by the wind, because the leaves moved through the air.
explain: The same word can mean something very different in another sentence. «The lights went out because a fuse had blown.» Here blown means broken suddenly, like a fuse that has burst. Ask yourself: which meaning fits this sentence? Then try it in the sentence to check.
explain: Blown also appears in phrases. «We blew up the red balloons for the party.» Blown up means filled with air, like a balloon. «The bomb blew up» would mean it exploded. Look at the words around blown to find which meaning the writer wants.
fact: Blown is the past form of the verb blow: blow, blew, blown.
fact: «Blown» can mean moved or pushed by wind or air, as in «The hat was blown off my head».
fact: «Blown» can mean broken suddenly, as in «a blown fuse» or «a blown tyre».
fact: «Blown glass» is glass shaped by blowing air into it.
fact: «Blown up» can mean exploded, or filled with air like a balloon.
exercise: «The hat was blown off his head by the strong wind.» What does blown mean here? | Filled with air like a balloon | Broken suddenly, like a fuse | Made from glass | *Moved by the wind
exercise: «The kitchen light stopped working because the fuse had blown.» What does blown mean here? | *Broken suddenly | Blown up, like a balloon | Made by blowing | Moved by the wind
exercise: Which phrase means filled with air, like a balloon? | Blown over | Blown glass | *Blown up | Blown fuse
test: «The vase is made of blown glass.» What does blown glass mean? | Glass moved by the wind | Glass that has been broken suddenly | *Glass shaped by blowing air into it | Glass that is very old
test: «Dad said the tyre had blown, so we walked to school.» What does blown mean here? | Moved by the wind | *Burst suddenly | Filled with air | Made of glass
exam: «After the storm, several trees were blown over in the park.» What does blown over mean? | Painted bright blue | Made of glass | *Knocked down by the wind | Lost forever
